-                            <h4><strong>Saskadena Six Trails are Currently Closed to all traffic due to the ongoing snowmaking pipeline project.&nbsp;</strong></h4><p><em>Please enjoy the other local biking and hiking trail networks this summer!</em></p><p><a name="_Hlk211255736"></a></p>
+                            <p><strong>Wednesday, February 11th, 9am</strong></p><p><strong>New Snow: 4" Season Total: 57"</strong></p><p><strong>Primary Surface: Packed Powder/Powder</strong></p><p><strong>Trails: 24 Lifts: 2</strong></p><p><strong>Operating Day #42</strong></p><p>Good morning S6 skiers and riders! We received 3-4" of new snow across the hill last night and its a packed powder paradise out there this morning. It's a mix of powder and packed powder out there this morning and the majority of the groomers were done after the new snow and are skiing beautifully. Fresh turns can be found this morning on all the ungroomed terrain and we're skiing and riding on 24 trails serviced by Chair One and the conveyor lift in the learning area. Lifts turn today 9am-4pm. &nbsp;</p><p>Expansion into the Milky Way terrain park is expected tomorrow which will also open Backdoor, Standard and Spring Pine Glade bringing us to 100% open heading into the holiday week. We are now open daily through February 22nd including Monday &amp; Tuesday, February 16th &amp; 17th. This Saturday is the annual torchlight parade which starts at 6:30pm.&nbsp;</p><p>Uphill access is &nbsp;open on Easy Mile and the Easy Mile Woods Route. As a reminder, all uphill travelers will need to register with Uphill New England this season and will be required to wear an identifying armband. Downhill passholders may do so by requesting an access code from the ticket office or by email to&nbsp;<a href="mailto:s6info@woodstockinn.com">s6info@woodstockinn.com</a>. Those looking to purchase an uphill only pass may do so by&nbsp;<a href="https://www.uphillnewengland.org/product-page/saskadena-six-uphill-season-pass" target="_blank">CLICKING HERE</a>. Be sure to familiarize yourself with the uphill guidelines and routes and always use appropriate equipment. There is no foot traffic or snowshoeing permitted down the trails. &nbsp;<a href="https://www.saskadenasix.com/UPHILL" target="_blank">https://www.saskadenasix.com/UPHILL</a></p><p>&nbsp;Be sure to check out the new Perley’s Pourhouse bar menu serving lunch daily along side delicious cocktails and craft brews 11am-5pm. The Corduroy Café is open throughout the day with breakfast starting at 9am and lunch at 11am.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Mountain Hours of Operation:</strong><br>Open Daily Through 2/22 (Open 2/16 &amp; 2/17)</p><p>Non Peak Hours: Wednesday – Sunday, 9am-4pm</p><p><em><strong>Closed Monday/Tuesday Non-Peak</strong></em><br><em>Peak dates: 2/14/26 thru 2/22/26</em><br><strong>Retail Shop Hours of Operation:</strong><br>Open All Operating Days: 9am–4pm<br><strong>Perley’s Pourhouse:</strong><br>Open All Operating Days: 11am-5pm<br><strong>Corduroy Cafe:</strong><br>Open All Operating Days: 9am-4pm&nbsp;</p><p><a name="_Hlk211255736"></a><strong>2025-26 RACE DATES:</strong></p><p><span>Thursday 2/19/26 GTS M/W SL – 9am</span></p><p><span>Sunday 3/1/26 MVC U10 – 9am</span></p><p><span>Sunday 3/8/26 Masters of the MTN&nbsp;</span></p>
             
 
